From aec08dcb724752a30436680f3b5654715e6e2da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:31:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Volume and brightness sliders

Buttons with Command = "VolumeSlider" / "BrightnessSlider" open a slider
over the row, right of Esc: a close button, the button's icon and a track,
as on macOS. A tap opens it for SliderTimeout ms (default 3000); on the
track the knob jumps to the finger and follows it, and each touch starts
the timeout again. Holding the button and sliding moves the value from
where it was, and the buttons come back on release. Only Esc stays usable
under the slider.

tiny-dfr runs as nobody and cannot set the volume or the brightness the
way the desktop does, so it hands the value to a helper in the session
through the FIFO /run/tiny-dfr/bridge/cmd, at most every 30 ms while the
finger moves and always on release; the volume to start from comes from
/run/tiny-dfr/bridge/volume, the brightness from the display backlight.
Without the helper the slider sends volume/brightness keys instead, one
per 5 % of the track. The slider is drawn over the row after it and only
its own area is sent to the panel while it moves.

The PNG preview adds rows with the sliders open.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
